From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Paper Linux contributors <paper-linux@localhost>
Date: Tue, 12 Aug 2026 00:00:00 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] mdev: restore device scan for pre-2.6.27 kernels

BusyBox commit 20a3262cd756 (mdev: create devices from /sys/dev)
removed the /sys/class and legacy /sys/block coldplug scan.  Linux
2.6.26 and older do not provide /sys/dev, so mdev -s creates no device
nodes on vendor kernels of that age.

BusyBox's published advice for these kernels is to revert that commit.
Retain the current /sys/dev scan on newer kernels and restore the same
legacy scan as a runtime fallback when /sys/dev is absent.  This keeps
the intervening mdev fixes while following the upstream compatibility
recommendation.

Upstream advice:
https://busybox.net/oldnews.html#2017-03-31-10:42

Signed-off-by: Paper Linux contributors <paper-linux@localhost>
---
 util-linux/mdev.c | 27 ++++++++++++++++++++++-----
 1 file changed, 22 insertions(+), 5 deletions(-)

diff --git a/util-linux/mdev.c b/util-linux/mdev.c
--- a/util-linux/mdev.c
+++ b/util-linux/mdev.c
@@ -1143,10 +1143,25 @@ static void initial_scan(char *temp)
 
 	putenv((char*)"ACTION=add");
 
-	/* Create all devices from /sys/dev hierarchy */
-	recursive_action("/sys/dev",
-			 ACTION_RECURSE | ACTION_FOLLOWLINKS,
-			 fileAction, dirAction, temp);
+	if (access("/sys/dev", F_OK) == 0) {
+		/* Linux 2.6.27 and newer provide a complete major:minor index. */
+		recursive_action("/sys/dev",
+				 ACTION_RECURSE | ACTION_FOLLOWLINKS,
+				 fileAction, dirAction, temp);
+	} else {
+		/* Linux 2.6.26 and older have no /sys/dev hierarchy.  Restore
+		 * the scan used before BusyBox commit 20a3262: class devices,
+		 * plus the legacy block hierarchy when class/block is absent.
+		 */
+		if (access("/sys/class/block", F_OK) != 0) {
+			recursive_action("/sys/block",
+					 ACTION_RECURSE | ACTION_FOLLOWLINKS | ACTION_QUIET,
+					 fileAction, dirAction, temp);
+		}
+		recursive_action("/sys/class",
+				 ACTION_RECURSE | ACTION_FOLLOWLINKS,
+				 fileAction, dirAction, temp);
+	}
 }
 
 #if ENABLE_FEATURE_MDEV_DAEMON
-- 
